WEBVTT

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
The Past Revealed

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
The Heartless Gizmon:AT!

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.550
The Past Revealed!

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.550
The Heartless Gizmon:AT!

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:25.940
Yukidarumon

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:25.940
Adult Level

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.780
Yukidarumon.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.140
An Adult Level Digimon made up of snow and ice.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.940
Although appearing cold on the outside, she actually has a warm, gentle personality and dislikes fighting.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.670
Oh my.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.890
There, there.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.360
Ikuto!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.790
Ikuto!!

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.050
Iku... to?

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.220
So...

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.550
You're called Ikuto.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.510
Ikuto!!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.290
This isn't good.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:07.370
There, there.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.440
Want to come along with me?

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.650
Oh, you do?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.970
You can't fight!

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.900
Aniki is in the middle of a man-to-man fight right now!

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.110
You can't!

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.650
Don't interfere with him!

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.930
I won't allow fighting!

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.090
Geez...

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.250
Mercurimon!

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.380
I met my mother in the human world!

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.090
I...

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.540
I wasn't really a Digimon, right?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.840
I'm human, right?!

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.280
Yes.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.930
You are human.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.940
You were born in a world that is alien from ours.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.020
That doesn't give you the right to try and kill him!

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.700
What do you mean?

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.140
Don't play dumb!

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.080
Gotsumon brought along a bunch of other Digimon and attacked him!

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.840
I didn't give that order.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:01.620
What?

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.840
Do you mean Gotsumon decided to do that on his own?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.900
There are many among the Digimon who hate humans to the extreme.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.040
Gotsumon was one of them.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.160
I used to hate humans, too.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:13.750
But...

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.600
When I met Masaru and the others, I realized...

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.080
not all humans are bad.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:19.720
Ikuto...

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.570
What's most important, I got to become friends with Falcomon.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:27.720
Humans and Digimon don't need to fight, do they?

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.660
Friends, you say?

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.270
You must be kidding me.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:40.650
Digimon are dangerous beasts who only inflict harm upon human beings.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.160
You!

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.790
What are <i>you</i>  doing here?!

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.610
It can't be...

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.370
Did you bring him with you?

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.340
I've misjudged you, Daimon Masaru!

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.550
What do you mean?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.800
Don't try to fool me!

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.890
That man is the very one who killed our comrades, including Yukidarumon!

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:11.490
Wh-What?!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.010
Mercurimon-sama, this way!

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.510
It's been awhile, Yukidarumon.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.060
What are you, one of the Olympus Twelve, doing in a place like this?

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.330
I've come to pull out the roots of calamity before they sprout.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:39.620
Calamity?

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.020
He means this child!

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.900
Digimon and humans were never originally meant to interact with one another.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.430
Now, hand over that child to me.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.620
Despite it being your orders, this is one I refuse to listen to!

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.290
What?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.200
This child... Ikuto, I will raise him!

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.100
I've already made up my mind about this!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:58.750
H-Hey!

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.900
How dare you use that tone of voice towards Mercurimon-sama!

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.950
There, there.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.270
I've heard of this.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.620
Human mothers act this way towards their children to protect them.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.890
Do you intend to be that child's mother?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.610
Mother?

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.710
Mother...

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.710
I like the sound of that.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:25.280
All right.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.860
Starting today, I will be Ikuto's mother!

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:38.310
Yukidarumon loved Ikuto from the bottom of her heart...

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.620
just as if he were her real son.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.300
But that man ripped apart the bond between Ikuto and Yukidarumon!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.860
Don't be fooled by his one-sided excuse of a story.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.850
The real victim is actually me.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.180
What do you mean by that?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:06.980
When the Digital World Exploration Squad was formed ten years ago...

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:12.620
the Digimon had almost taken our lives.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.880
Daimon Suguru

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.880
Professor of
Supra-organisms

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.590
They're magnificent!

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.090
Professor Daimon, please be more serious about this!

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.260
We've come here to search for Ikuto-kun!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.720
Satsuma Rentarou

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.720
Kanagawa Police HQ

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.720
Detective of
Special Investigations

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.800
Now, now, Satsuma-kun.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.000
I can't blame the Professor.

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.430
Yushima Hiroshi

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.430
Kanagawa Police HQ

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.430
Assistant Inspector of
Special Investigations

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.970
This world is full of things I've never seen before.

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:41.100
That's exactly right!

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.520
This place is truly magnificent!

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:47.890
S-Stay away from me!

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.940
Stay away!

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:50.780
Don't shoot, Kurata!

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:51.450
Throw your gun down!

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.170
Why did you shoot?

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.020
You have to ask?!

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.590
That thing was about to attack me!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.300
As long as we don't appear threatening to them, they'll leave us alone!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.600
Look!

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.230
It thinks we're its enemy!

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:23.900
Not good!

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:24.950
Run!

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:30.320
Satsuma-san!

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.870
Ever since then, our days grew hellish.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:41.450
As we trembled from constant fear of Digimon attack, we entered this Infinity Ice Ridge to try and take refuge.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:47.880
You won't escape, filthy humans!

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.160
Over here!

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.320
Now that it's come to this...

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.090
That's...

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.310
The space-time oscillation bomb.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.530
We can use this to force the Digital Gate to open!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.370
 Don't! That thing hasn't been finalized.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.480
It's too dangerous!

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.910
This is the only choice we have if we want to survive!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.940
It was a really close call.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:37.770
If the space-time oscillation bomb had exploded a second later,

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:43.110
I'm sure we would have been ripped to pieces by the vicious Digimon.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:46.280
That's right, you coward!

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.930
You ran off!

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.070
But that man didn't.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.280
He tackled me from the front and kept up a tough fight to the very end.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.530
By "that man," you can't mean...

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.740
My dad?!

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:13.620
Professor!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.640
I'll stay here to stop him.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.050
Everyone, escape now while you still can!

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.960
Impossible...

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.970
How can a human have so much power?

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:26.480
When a man wants to protect something, he can find hidden strength within him.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.400
Just like you have your reason to fight...

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.720
I have friends that I must protect!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.850
How interesting!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.620
I shall fight you!

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.580
No matter who it is, I won't hold back!

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.650
Th-That is so cool!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.790
Hey, hear that?!

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:59.760
My dad fought with Mercurimon!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.580
Yeah!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:02.430
That's just what you'd expect from Aniki's dad.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.380
He's amazing, in all implications of the word.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:04.720
Yeah.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.360
Suguru was strong.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:11.140
Even in front of me, his heart never faltered.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.570
Why have you stepped onto the sacred grounds of the Digital World?

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.620
Because an unknown wind was blowing here.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.240
A wind?

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.930
I want to know the unknown.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.670
I want to see whatever I wish!

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.050
That curiosity is a man's instinct!

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:32.690
It's a natural desire!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:39.010
Are you saying that satisfying that desire gives you the right to trample down and devastate our world?

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.010
We never meant to do that!

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.470
Suguru explained his situation to me,

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:48.850
and I learned about how the Digital Gate made sudden appearances in his world,

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:51.940
causing a large number of humans to disappear without a trace.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:57.480
Also, that he himself had come looking for the child of one of his friends, who had been sucked into the Gate.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.310
Was that Ikuto?

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.330
Yes.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:04.410
I believed Suguru's words and told him everything.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:05.900
What?

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.290
You know Ikuto?

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.350
Yes.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.540
One of my comrades is raising him dearly.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.410
I see! So he's okay!

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.500
Noguchi's gonna be happy to hear this.

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.110
Noguchi?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.640
That's Ikuto's father.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.460
Father?

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.480
I have a son, too.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.630
His name's Masaru and he's a naughty boy.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:26.040
Kids are great.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.430
They always look at you with a direct gaze.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:33.400
While you try teaching them how to live, you always end up learning something from them instead.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.570
Suguru.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.230
Go meet Yggdrasil.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.400
Yggdrasil?

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.450
He is a being that can be considered the God of the Digital World.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:49.950
In order to get humans and Digimon to live in harmony, you'll need Yggdrasil's approval first.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.080
I see.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.170
Well, where is this Yggdrasil?

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.630
He is everywhere and yet nowhere.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.590
Are you making fun of me?

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.720
No, it's as I said.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.260
Yggdrasil is a god.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:09.260
You can feel God, but you cannot see His form.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:10.970
I see.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.440
I'd like to help you...

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:18.870
but with this thing here, I can't leave this place.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:23.240
Any comrade of mine who knows nothing of it could get too close and fall into the human world.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.210
I'm sorry.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.240
Don't worry. It's not your fault.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:28.160
Let's make one!

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.170
A world where Digimon and humans can live together!

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.910
Yeah, let's do it!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.340
Suguru went on a journey in search of Yggdrasil.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:44.300
However, we haven't heard from him since.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:48.890
He may be lying dead somewhere in this world.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.020
Don't be stupid!

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.350
Dad isn't dead!

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:56.310
He's definitely alive somewhere in the Digital World!

00:12:57.990 --> 00:12:59.770
Professor Daimon is indeed alive.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:06.490
The blueprint of the Digivice that we received from the Digital World is solid proof of that.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:11.130
At the same time, the Professor entrusted both Kamemon and me with a message before we were sent here.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:17.170
We were to cooperate with humans and create an organization that provided protection to any Digimon who came wandering into the human world.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.200
And what was established was...

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:23.130
Digital Accident Tactics Squad -

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:24.590
DATS!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.550
So, it was Dad who made the Digivices?

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.600
I get it!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:37.480
Now I understand why there isn't any data for Kudamon or Kamemon in HQ's database.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:41.550
That's because in order to fulfill Professor Daimon's wishes...

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:47.960
they arrived from the Digital World as special emissaries, to prevent other Digimon from attacking the humans!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.870
The Digimon who unfortunately roamed into the human world...

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:02.520
were turned into Digieggs and transferred back to the Digital World.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:08.380
I continued to sit in front of the Digital Gate during those times.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.340
But that peace was destroyed.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:16.030
That man brought his comrades with him, and attacked the Digital World!

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:47.840
It's showtime!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.630
Humans are attacking?

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.660
Mercurimon-sama!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.590
That Suguru...

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.040
He betrayed me!

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.250
What's that?

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.960
I think it's near your house.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.000
Yukidarumon...

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.010
We won't let you do what you please!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:49.070
A-Anyone who invades the Digital World...

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.190
Will never be forgiven!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.940
What little pests you are.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:56.660
You pathetic Digimon think you can defy humans?

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:00.800
Let me show you my greatest masterpiece!

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:03.120
Gizmon, Realize!

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:11.960
What are they?

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.260
Are they Digimon, too?

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.450
No way!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:20.190
Their Digieggs aren't even left behind!

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.690
What are you doing?!

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.150
Ikuto hasn't come back yet!

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.860
There's no time to be worrying about that!

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.630
Yukidarumon!

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.720
Yukidarumon!

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:50.430
Ikuto, don't come here!

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:51.760
Run!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.970
Yukidarumon!!!

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:02.780
Reporting in!

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.090
There are several Digimon who are resisting in the western sector.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.730
They're giving the third platoon a hard fight.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.690
Send the second platoon to the western sector.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:10.900
Yes, sir!

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:18.280
If we leave these vicious monsters alone, they'll come to attack the human world someday.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:19.910
All Digimon must be eradicated!

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:23.160
A large Digimon signal is heading in this direction.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:25.460
Thousand Fist!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.150
I-Impossible!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.780
My greatest masterpieces were destroyed in an instant!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.260
Wretched human, why did you break your promise?!

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:38.780
Unforgivable!

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.070
Ikuto...

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.580
Ikuto... I can't go any further...

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:57.780
This is farewell.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.490
Run away quickly, you two!

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.750
I don't want to!

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:05.400
We take Yukidarumon with us!

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.360
Listen to me carefully, Ikuto.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:19.520
A sad and painful fate may be in store for you from now on.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:21.640
But Ikuto...

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.850
You must never hate the humans...

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.280
Because, you are...

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.280
Mom...

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.720
Mom!

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.410
MOM!!!

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.380
This is Ikuto's fault.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.110
What are you talking about, Gotsumon?

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.920
What did Ikuto ever do?!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:00.510
Strange things have occurred in this forest ever since Ikuto came here!

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.790
I knew it all along, you <i>are</i>  the root of calamity!

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.430
Leave this forest right now!

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:06.260
No!

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.240
Ikuto didn't do anything wrong!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.240
Right, guys?

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.450
Guys!

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:14.610
No way...

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:18.180
Ikuto!

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:24.420
Even if Ikuto left now, Yukidarumon will not return to us.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.160
But Mercurimon-sama!

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.580
It is Yukidarumon's dying wish that you shoulder the destiny that befalls this forest.

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.130
Ikuto, live in this forest.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.250
As the Digital World's warrior!

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:51.990
I am Digimon!

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:54.140
The Digital World's warrior...

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:55.190
Ikuto!

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.940
This guy killed Yukidarumon?!

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:03.260
Yes, Ikuto!

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.320
This is the man who killed your mother!

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.450
"Mother?"

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.300
What do you mean by that?

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.750
To humans, <i>all</i>  Digimon are the enemy!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:19.710
I'm merely fulfilling my mission to protect us against the demonic hand of the evil Digimon!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:22.550
Your story isn't a very logical one.

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.210
Ikuto's hatred and Mercurimon's hatred...

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:29.010
All of it was caused by you?!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:31.980
What will you do if it was?

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:36.450
Will you, as DATS members, attack me?

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:38.480
That's quite strange.

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.200
You're the lowest of the low, you bastard!

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.680
You're a goddamned disgrace of a man to the entire human race!

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.320
You can't even gather the nerve to get rid of one Digimon.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.730
All you do is flap your mouths.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:49.900
What a disaster.

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:54.070
I'd have preferred things to end with you and Mercurimon striking each other down.

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:55.620
I'm very disappointed.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.130
Mercurimon!

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:09.790
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for waiting!

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:14.680
These are my greatest masterpieces, Gizmon:AT!

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:24.350
Kurata!

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:27.610
Aniki, I've never felt this pissed off in my entire life!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:34.440
You are <i>not</i>  getting away with this!

